# Real credentials - only Network_Mapper/lib/Auth.example.json (placeholder template) is
# tracked. The real Auth.json a user creates from it lives next to Start-NetworkMapper.ps1
# (its default -AuthFile ".\Auth.json" is CWD-relative, and Network_Mapper/ is where you'd
# actually invoke that script from), not in lib/ with the template.
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Mapper/Auth.json

# Scraper output - contains real internal topology/IP data, not fixtures. Every real crawl
# writes into the shared Network_Maps/ folder (see Start-NetworkMapper.ps1's $SnapshotDir),
# named NetworkMap_<timestamp>.json(.enc) or ...tmp... while a write is in progress. The two
# shipped sample snapshots happen to follow that same naming convention on purpose (so
# "Load Folder of Snapshots" can load them together to demo the multi-snapshot/diff
# features) - the explicit `!` exceptions below are the only tracked files matching the
# pattern; any OTHER NetworkMap_*.json(.enc) is real crawl output and stays ignored.
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_*.json
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_*.json.enc
!PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_2026-08-13_091500.json
!PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_2026-08-20_143207.json
!PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_2026-08-20_143207.json.enc
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Mapper/Mapper_Debug.log
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Mapper/RawDumps/

# PS_NetworkMapper_V2's Auth.json, Network_Maps/, and NDJSON device-history ledger are
# not duplicated here - V2 shares all of that with PS_NetworkMapper/ above (see
# Start-NetworkMapper.ps1's $AuthFile/$SnapshotDir defaults). Only its own per-run debug
# artifacts are local to it.
PS_NetworkMapper_V2/Network_Mapper/Mapper_Debug.log
PS_NetworkMapper_V2/Network_Mapper/RawDumps/
